From: Armada <armada@armada.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: ufs: allow Eliza legacy doorbell mode

The Retroid Pocket Duo uses the Eliza controller with a UFS 2.2 device
in single-doorbell mode. Its board description deliberately omits the
MCQ register range so the existing driver falls back to that mode.
Allow Eliza to use the common one-or-two-region constraint; keep the
mandatory MCQ range for Nord.

Reference: RetroidPocket/linux commit 314716524ae09a942064a3dd2008042b3e4b2f85.
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,sm8650-ufshc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,sm8650-ufshc.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,sm8650-ufshc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/ufs/qcom,sm8650-ufshc.yaml
@@ -77,7 +77,6 @@
         compatible:
           contains:
             enum:
-              - qcom,eliza-ufshc
               - qcom,nord-ufshc
     then:
       properties:
